1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,667
Here's how to get started with ShellX, from your first workspace to answering your AI agents

2
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:06,549
from your phone.

3
00:00:07,988 --> 00:00:13,335
Install ShellX on your Mac or Windows PC. Each project lives in its own workspace,

4
00:00:13,335 --> 00:00:16,073
listed in the sidebar under Your Machines.

5
00:00:16,566 --> 00:00:22,639
Open a new one with the plus button. The sidebar shows each workspace's git branch,

6
00:00:22,639 --> 00:00:25,127
folder and open ports at a glance.

7
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:30,218
Split any workspace into panes, to the right or down.

8
00:00:30,909 --> 00:00:35,790
Run your dev server in one pane, and preview the app in the built-in browser right next to it.

9
00:00:39,102 --> 00:00:42,764
Every action is in the command palette. Press Command Shift P,

10
00:00:42,764 --> 00:00:44,122
and type what you need.

11
00:00:49,332 --> 00:00:54,150
Now start Claude Code, Codex, or any command-line AI agent in a pane,

12
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:55,966
just like in any terminal.

13
00:01:03,370 --> 00:01:07,164
ShellX follows what the agent is doing. When it needs your permission,

14
00:01:07,164 --> 00:01:11,664
the workspace is flagged in the sidebar, and your paired phone gets a notification.

15
00:01:12,157 --> 00:01:14,820
Approve it here, and the agent carries on.

16
00:01:23,461 --> 00:01:27,539
To take your sessions with you, pair your phone. On your Mac,

17
00:01:27,539 --> 00:01:31,082
open Settings, choose Mobile, and click Show QR Code.

18
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:43,417
In ShellX on your phone, open Settings, then Your Macs,

19
00:01:43,417 --> 00:01:47,715
and tap plus. Scan the code, or paste the pairing code.

20
00:01:48,193 --> 00:01:51,918
Check the Mac's name, tap Pair, and allow the phone on your Mac.

21
00:01:51,918 --> 00:01:54,653
Only devices you allow can reach your sessions.

22
00:01:55,901 --> 00:01:59,558
Every workspace from every paired Mac shows up on your phone,

23
00:01:59,558 --> 00:02:01,177
with its branch and status.

24
00:02:02,801 --> 00:02:08,332
Tap one to follow the agent live. Type a message, and it goes straight to the session on your Mac.

25
00:02:10,901 --> 00:02:14,760
Then watch it write the code and run the tests, as it happens.

26
00:02:17,897 --> 00:02:22,139
Needs You collects every request from your agents in one place.

27
00:02:22,635 --> 00:02:25,171
Allow a command with one tap.

28
00:02:25,649 --> 00:02:29,299
Answer a question by picking an option, or by voice.

29
00:02:33,197 --> 00:02:36,897
And review a plan before any code is written. Approve it,

30
00:02:36,897 --> 00:02:40,597
revise it, or deny it, without walking back to your desk.

31
00:02:42,146 --> 00:02:45,834
All of this is end-to-end encrypted between your devices.

32
00:02:45,834 --> 00:02:50,752
The ShellX relay only forwards encrypted bytes: it can't read your terminal,

33
00:02:50,752 --> 00:02:52,240
and it never stores it.

34
00:02:53,786 --> 00:02:58,719
That's ShellX. Download it free for Mac and Windows at shellx.pro,

35
00:02:58,719 --> 00:03:02,382
and get the app for your iPhone or Android phone.
